openxlr for Ubuntu
------------------

After installing:

 1. Replug your interface once so the udev rule applies.
 2. Log out and back in, or run  systemctl --user restart wireplumber,
    so the packaged WirePlumber rules load.
 3. Start the daemon:  systemctl --user enable --now openxlr-daemon
 4. Start the mixer:   openxlr   (or from your application menu)

On GNOME on Wayland, routing the focused application needs the packaged
OpenXLR Focus extension:  gnome-extensions enable openxlr-focus@emaspa.github.com
and a new login.

Packages built for WirePlumber 0.4, including Ubuntu 24.04, include an owned
node state rule under /usr/share/wireplumber/main.lua.d. It keeps old desktop
volume and mute values from replacing OpenXLR's saved software mixer state.
After installing or upgrading such a package, load the rule at your next
login, or restart these services from your desktop session when you can
interrupt audio:

    systemctl --user restart wireplumber
    systemctl --user restart openxlr-daemon

The package does not restart these services automatically. WirePlumber 0.5
honors the node declaration directly; packages built for 0.5 omit the Lua rule.

Stream Deck control via OpenDeck:

    mkdir -p ~/.config/opendeck/plugins
    cp -r /usr/share/openxlr/com.emaspa.openxlr.sdPlugin \
        ~/.config/opendeck/plugins/

The software ClipGuard limiter for the XLR Dock needs the SWH LADSPA
plugins (package: swh-plugins). The daemon picks them up from the
standard LADSPA path. Without that optional package the ClipGuard control
is disabled; all other controls and the existing microphone route continue
to work.

Inserts on XLR inputs and mixes support LV2, CLAP and VST3. The package
includes the native helper for CLAP/VST3 and plugin editors. Install
compatible plugins separately; lsp-plugins-lv2 supplies LV2 effects.
Windows VST3/CLAP additionally need Wine and yabridge. The optional
openxlr-yabridge companion has a separate build/artifact workflow and
private wrappers; it is not automatically installed with openxlr.

Manual and bridge setup:
https://github.com/emaspa/openxlr/blob/main/docs/manual.md#windows-plugins
For matching release documentation, select the installed version's tag.
